''Human Host'' ships with mod-friendly infrastructure and includes '''[https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx BepInEx]''' 5.4.23.2 pre-installed. All game assemblies are pure Mono with debug symbols (PDBs) shipped, making decompilation and Harmony patching straightforward.

This page covers the technical modding surface. For installed mods (community-authored plugins), see '''[[Mods]]'''.

== Prerequisites ==

* Game version 5.4.x or later (BepInEx already bundled)
* Windows (only officially supported platform)
* For plugin authors: '''.NET SDK 8+''', '''ILSpy''' or '''dnSpy''' for decompilation

== Installing mods ==

# Drop the plugin `.dll` into `<Steam>/steamapps/common/Human Host/BepInEx/plugins/`
# Launch the game. BepInEx auto-loads any plugin in this folder.
# Check `BepInEx/LogOutput.log` for load errors.

== Writing your own mod ==

The game exposes '''every major system''' through a central hub singleton (<code>Mgr_Hub._ins</code>). From there you can reach:

{| class="wikitable"
! Manager !! Purpose
|-
| <code>Skill_Mgr._ins</code> || Perk / skill trees, factor multipliers
|-
| <code>Loot_Mgr._ins</code> || Container windows, inventory
|-
| <code>Craft_Mgr._ins</code> || Recipe registry
|-
| <code>Trap_Mgr._ins</code> || Trap registration
|-
| <code>Terrain_Dig._ins</code> || Mining events
|-
| <code>World_Map_Mgr._CompassPro</code> || Minimap POI registration
|-
| <code>Player_HotKeys._ins</code> || Hotkey rebinding
|-
| <code>SaveDataManager</code> || Save-slot events
|}

Recommended patterns:

* Use '''Harmony''' postfixes for anything on a manager entry point.
* Register additions (perks, recipes, POIs, layers) through the game's own registration methods rather than mutating collections directly.
* Persist your mod state via a sidecar file next to `Save_XX/` rather than injecting into the game save.

== Lua vehicle programming ==

Vehicles accept player Lua scripts via <code>Car_Coding.LoadPlayerCode(string)</code>. This is technically a mod surface (arbitrary logic per vehicle tick), but it's an in-game feature exposed to players, not a BepInEx path. See [[Lua Programming]].

== Asset bundles ==

Game assets ship as Unity Addressables in `Human Host_Data/StreamingAssets/aa/StandaloneWindows64/`. There are 79 bundles, split by category (biomes, weapons, vehicles, POIs, etc.). Modders wanting to inspect asset data can use '''AssetRipper''' or '''UABE'''.

